# A net diagram intentionally does not pretend to be a spatial route.
svg='''<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 575" role="img" aria-label="20 volt input, 5 volt converter, three motor power zones and separate logic supplies"><defs><marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="#d86137"/></marker></defs><g fill="#fff" stroke="#b7c6ce" stroke-width="2"><rect x="25" y="25" width="205" height="75" rx="12"/><rect x="285" y="25" width="205" height="75" rx="12"/><rect x="545" y="25" width="245" height="75" rx="12"/><rect x="105" y="230" width="230" height="85" rx="12"/><rect x="435" y="230" width="230" height="85" rx="12"/><rect x="765" y="230" width="230" height="85" rx="12"/><rect x="95" y="425" width="260" height="95" rx="12"/><rect x="425" y="425" width="250" height="95" rx="12"/><rect x="765" y="425" width="230" height="95" rx="12"/></g><g stroke="#d86137" fill="none" stroke-width="4" marker-end="url(#arrow)"><path d="M230 62H285"/><path d="M490 62H545"/><path d="M665 100V160H220V230"/><path d="M665 160H550V230"/><path d="M665 160H880V230"/><path d="M665 160H1030V382H225V425"/><path d="M550 382V425"/><path d="M880 382V425"/></g><g font-family="Arial,sans-serif" fill="#18363f" text-anchor="middle"><text x="127" y="54" font-size="18" font-weight="bold">MDY-14-ED + 5991</text><text x="127" y="79" font-size="15">20 V request · external</text><text x="388" y="54" font-size="18" font-weight="bold">DFR1202</text><text x="388" y="79" font-size="15">5 V · original battery bay</text><text x="667" y="54" font-size="18" font-weight="bold">Paired distribution joints</text><text x="667" y="79" font-size="15">5 V and common return</text><text x="220" y="263" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Left leg · IDs 5 → 1</text><text x="550" y="263" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Right leg · IDs 10 → 6</text><text x="880" y="263" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Head / neck · 15 → 12</text><text x="220" y="292" font-size="15">Own paired feed · five motors</text><text x="550" y="292" font-size="15">Own paired feed · five motors</text><text x="880" y="292" font-size="15">15, 14, 13, 11, 12</text><text x="225" y="458" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Pi Zero W</text><text x="225" y="484" font-size="15">5 V: pins 2 + 4 · GND: 6 + 14</text><text x="225" y="506" font-size="14">Camera via CSI · IMU via 3.3 V</text><text x="550" y="458" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">OpenRB</text><text x="550" y="484" font-size="15">J4 5 V/GND · VIN(DXL) jumper</text><text x="550" y="506" font-size="14">No motor power through DXL ports</text><text x="880" y="458" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">MAX98357A</text><text x="880" y="484" font-size="15">VIN/GND paired branch</text><text x="880" y="506" font-size="14">Speaker on +/− outputs only</text><text x="550" y="555" font-size="16">Orange lines represent paired power circuits. All returns meet at the distribution ground.</text></g></svg>'''
(D/'power-topology.svg').write_text(svg)
phase_html=''.join('<article class="step"><h3>'+str(i+1)+'. '+html.escape(s['title'])+'</h3>'+''.join('<section><h4>'+phase.title()+'</h4><ol>'+''.join('<li>'+html.escape(t)+'</li>' for t in s[phase])+'</ol></section>' for phase in ['prepare','assemble','check'])+'</article>' for i,s in enumerate(steps))
source_html=''.join('<li><a href="'+x['url']+'">'+html.escape(x['id'])+'</a>: '+html.escape(x['fact'])+'</li>' for x in sources)
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>MicroDuck · Power and body wiring</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#edf2f4;color:#19313a;font:17px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:36px 22px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,54px);line-height:1.12;margin:10px 0 24px}h2{margin-top:42px}h3{margin:0 0 18px}h4{font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#276779;margin:15px 0 5px}p{max-width:900px}.kicker{color:#36727d;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em}.summary,.step,.diagram{background:white;border:1px solid #d4dfe3;border-radius:16px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.status{border-left:5px solid #c5882b;padding:12px 18px;background:#fff5de}.step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:0 24px}.step h3{grid-column:1/-1}.step li{margin:8px 0}ol{padding-left:22px}svg{width:100%;height:auto}a{color:#176c85}small{color:#506972}.detail{font-size:15px}.badges{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}.badges span{border:1px solid #bdced4;border-radius:30px;padding:6px 13px;font-size:14px}@media(max-width:760px){.step{display:block}.diagram{overflow:auto}.diagram svg{min-width:790px}}</style><main><div class="kicker">MICRODUCK · ENGINEERING / ASSEMBLY</div><h1>One source.<br>Three motor power zones.</h1><p>The external charger feeds the converter in the original battery bay. Separate paired feeds supply the two legs and head/neck; OpenRB carries motor data. The added eleven-fuse array has been removed from this design.</p><div class="badges"><span>Original body width</span><span>Eight leg cables retained</span><span>Pi → OpenRB USB retained</span><span>No new printed part for the checked body section</span></div><p class="status"><strong>Design status:</strong> converter-to-distribution body geometry is checked. Outgoing zone feeds, the final head/neck route and powered load testing remain open. This page does not certify the whole robot or make the current print package ready.</p><div class="diagram">'''+svg+'''<small>Electrical net diagram, not a spatial route. DATA crosses zone boundaries; VDD and load returns do not cross through the controller cable.</small></div><div class="summary"><h2 style="margin-top:0">What the ratings mean</h2><p>OpenRB’s four motor ports share <strong>3 A total</strong>. Each EH power path is rated <strong>3 A with AWG22</strong>. DFR1202’s <strong>16 A maximum</strong> does not raise either connector rating.</p><p>The commissioning proposal starts at <strong>450 mA per motor</strong> in a supported current-limited operating mode: 2.25 A per zone, 6.75 A motor total. Readback, startup measurement and real motion/load testing are required; software settings are not short-circuit protection. Five simultaneous nominal stalls would draw 7.35 A per zone, outside this operating envelope.</p><p>The existing whole-robot design budget remains <strong>9 A continuous / 9.5 A short peak</strong>, with a 2 A nonmotor reserve. No assertion is made that the trained policy delivers its required torque at the initial limit.</p></div><h2>Connect it in this order</h2>'''+phase_html+'''<h2>What is checked in the body</h2><p>The two output-pad leads and their insulated continuations use the actual registered DFR rear lands, the existing negative-Y opening, and two separate insulated joints above the original support. The new local check covers 666 wire/body pairs, 326 joint-space pairs and eight joint/wire pairs. Opposite polarities do not overlap. Only each joint’s own conductor is allowed inside its insulation receiving volume.</p><p>The two receiving joints are 6 × 12 mm maximum envelopes for bench-made, insulated soldered splices. They are not imaginary purchased terminal blocks. Stock wire, heat-shrink and termination consumables still need to be available; no purchase or sourcing hold has been released.</p><h2>Remaining installation boundaries</h2><ul><li>Complete the incoming VIN/tether termination and strain relief.</li><li>Place the three receiving-side motor injection adapters and set their actual lengths with motion slack.</li><li>Continue the accepted four IMU leads and power branches through the moving neck to the adopted head endpoints.</li><li>Inspect insulation, test polarity/continuity, and measure startup and representative loads before powered operation.</li></ul><h2>Sources and direct measurements</h2><ul class="detail">'''+source_html+'''</ul><small>Source verification: 9 October 2026. This page describes engineering requirements and digital local fit, not physical commissioning.</small></main></html>'''
(D/'POWER-WIRING.html').write_text(page)
print(json.dumps({'report':str(D/'integrated-harness.json'),'reportSha256':sha(D/'integrated-harness.json'),'page':str(D/'POWER-WIRING.html'),'manifest':str(D/'body-distribution-manifest.json')}))
